nt" sizes="100vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="hero-inner wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Fountain of Hope</a><span class="sep">/</span><a href="/#topics">Topics</a><span class="sep">/</span><span class="here">Topic 04</span></nav><div class="hero-kicker"><span style="color:#FF9CBE;font-weight:700">RECOGNITION · WOMEN&#x27;S HEALTH</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Garissa County</span></div><h1>An award that belongs to <em>the movement.</em></h1><p class="hero-sub">Recognition for years of work for the health of Garissa’s women — and for every woman of faith, every health worker and every mother whose strength made it possible.</p><div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn--pink" href="#story">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M19 12l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/#topics">All topics</a></div></div><div class="scroll-cue"><span class="line"></span>Scroll</div></section><section class="page-lead"><div class="wrap page-lead-inner"><p>Awards measure one moment, but the work they honor is measured in years. The recognition received for the health of Garissa’s women is a moment in the highlight reel of a much longer story — one written in meetings, radio calls, faith gatherings, dignity kits and mothers saved.</p></div></section><section class="fn-section" id="story"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv fn-head"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">The story</span><h2 class="h2">Recognition, and the <em>work behind it.</em></h2></div><p class="fn-intro">The award is a proud moment for Fountain of Hope — and for the women whose dedication made the work visible enough to be recognized at all.</p></div><div class="fn-editorial"><div class="rv fn-art"><img alt="A moment of recognition for women&#x27;s health in Garissa" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" sizes="60vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2FAward.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div><div class="rv fn-side"><div class="fn-card"><div class="no">— The story —</div><h3>Who the award really belongs to.</h3><p>When Fountain of Hope is recognized for the health of women, it is a recognition of<!-- --> <strong style="color:#fff">a whole movement</strong>: the women of faith who open their congregations, the health workers who extend a hand, and the mothers of Garissa who carry the message forward.</p><div class="fn-meta"><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 3h12l4 6-10 12L2 9l4-6Z"></path><path d="M12 3l2.5 4.6L12 21m0 0L9.5 7.6 12 3"></path><path d="M2 9h20"></path></svg><span><b class="bold">Recognition</b> in women’s health</span></div><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-5.5-7-11a7 7 0 1 1 14 0c0 5.5-7 11-7 11Z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="2.6"></circle></svg><span>Fountain of Hope <b class="bold">· Garissa, Kenya</b></span></div></div></div><div class="verify-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"></path></svg><span><b>Note for the team:</b> tone kept general; confirm the exact award name, date and occasion with the team before publishing.</span></div></div></div></div></section><section class="discuss" id="discuss"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv discuss-nav"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">The discussion, unpacked</span><h2>Recognition is a <em>milestone,</em> not a finish line.</h2><p>What the award celebrates — and what it asks next of us.</p></div><div class="rv discuss-body"><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">01</span> What the award honors</h3><p>The recognition speaks to the health of Garissa’s women — the<!-- --> <strong>very purpose of Fountain of Hope</strong> since 2017. It honors years of maternal and newborn survival work, of faith leaders carrying health messages into their congregations, and of women organizing around their own safety and dignity.</p></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">02</span> A moment in a longer story</h3><div class="dd-facts"><div class="fact"><div class="k">Started 2017</div><div class="v">A platform for Garissa’s women to advocate for their own<!-- --> <b>health, education and resilience</b> — founded by a daughter of Garissa.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">The work</div><div class="v">Maternal and newborn survival, girls’ education, clean water and <b>community-powered change</b> — visible enough to be recognized.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">The next chapter</div><div class="v">An award is not the end — it is<!-- --> <b>a measure of how far the movement has come</b>, and fuel for what still remains.</div></div></div></div><div class="dd-quote"><span class="qmark">“</span><blockquote>We are not just leaders in faith — we are leaders in life, and saving lives begins with us.</blockquote><div class="who">A woman religious leader · Garissa</div></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">03</span> Recognition belongs to Garissa’s women</h3><p>Every conversation about the award should end the same way it began: the recognition belongs to the<!-- --> <strong>women of Garissa</strong> — and the work continues until no mother, no child, no girl is left behind.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="related" id="related"><div class="wrap"><div class="rel-head rv"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">Keep exploring</span><h2 class="h2">More topics from <em>the field.</em></h2></div></div><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/okoamama-activity-05"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 01</div><h4>When a budget meeting is a life-saving meeting</h4><p>Garissa’s health executive and its budget-makers sit at one table to deliberate maternal and newborn health — and agree the way forward together.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/clean-water"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 03</div><h4>Clean water, and the dignity it brings</h4><p>Water, sanitation and hygiene work that protects mothers, children and whole communities in one of Kenya’s driest counties.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--navy);border-color:var(--navy)" href="/"><div class="rel-num" style="color:#FF9CBE">All topics</div><h4 style="color:#fff">Back to the Fountain of Hope story</h4><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.7)">Explore the full one-page story and every topic.</p><span class="lnk" style="color:#FF9CBE;margin-top:auto">Open the home page<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="rv cta-in"><span class="eyebrow">Support the work</span><h2>Stand with the women who <em>lead this change.</em></h2><p>Every recognition is a reminder of what the movement still needs — your support to keep going.</p><div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn--pink" href="/#footer">Donate now<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/#footer">Partner with us</a></div></div></section></main><footer id="footer"><div class="wrap"><div class="foot-grid"><div class="foot-about"><a class="brand" href="/#top"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path><pat